- op: create  # fdea
  at: '2026-05-28T07:34:03Z'  # fdea
  by: agent  # fdea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fdea
  clock: 1  # fdea
  nonce: fdea  # fdea
  data:  # fdea
    kind: invariant  # fdea
    title: "Solidity analyzer mis-classifies string literals (e.g. require messages) as imports"  # fdea
    status: violated  # fdea
    priority: 2  # fdea
    parent:  # fdea
    tags:  # fdea
    - dogfooding  # fdea
    - solidity  # fdea
    isbefore: []  # fdea
    duplicate_of: []  # fdea
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fdea
    pr_ref:  # fdea
    description: "**Symptom.** The Solidity analyzer emits `imports` edges to arbitrary string literals (e.g. `require()` revert messages) as if they were import paths. On hypergumbo self-analysis (branch dev @ 77a69627b8), the literal `\"Not owner\"` from `tests/fixtures/schema-coverage-corpus/solidity/Contract.sol:18` becomes:\n- a bogus external_symbol node: `{id: 'Not owner:<unknown>:0-0:Not owner:Not owner', kind: external_symbol, language: 'Not owner', name: 'Not owner', path: '<external>'}`\n- a bogus edge: `solidity:.../Contract.sol --imports--> 'Not owner:...'`\n- a leak into `io-boundaries.unsupported_languages`: `['Not owner', 'ansible', 'bash', 'csharp', ...]`\n- a leak into `verify-claims` INV-javam diagnostic: `Note: no taint-flow catalog for language(s): Not owner, ansible, ...`\n\n**Root cause.** `packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/src/hypergumbo_lang_extended1/solidity.py:355–369` iterates every node in the tree-sitter parse tree and unconditionally calls `_extract_import_aliases(node, source)`. That helper looks for any direct `\"string\"` child via `find_child_by_type(node, \"string\")`; if found, the string contents become the import path. Tree nodes like `call_argument` (which wraps `require`'s arguments) have a direct `\"string\"` child, so the function treats them as imports.\n\nThe indentation on lines 357–369 is 12 spaces deep inside an 8-space-block `for`, suggesting an earlier `if node.type == \"import_directive\":` guard was removed without re-indenting the body.\n\n**Fix sketch.**\n```python\nfor node in iter_tree(tree.root_node):\n    if node.type != \"import_directive\":\n        continue\n    import_path, aliases = _extract_import_aliases(node, source)\n    if import_path:\n        ...\n```\n\n**Blast radius.** On hypergumbo self-analysis: 1 spurious edge (one fixture). On real-world Solidity codebases: scales with `require(_, \"msg\")` / `revert(\"msg\")` / `emit Event(\"msg\")` etc. — likely tens to hundreds per contract.\n\n**Property test to lock down.** Every Solidity `imports` edge's `dst` must be a path that ends in `.sol` (or a relative-resolved Solidity file). Strings without that shape indicate the leak.\n\n**Discovery context.** Self-analysis dogfooding session, 2026-05-28. Lab notebook: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05282026_0707.md` (Finding B)."  # fdea
    fields:  # fdea
      statement: "The Solidity analyzer emits imports edges only from import_directive nodes; string literals inside call_expression / call_argument / emit / revert must not produce imports edges or external_symbol nodes."  # fdea
      root_cause: "solidity.py line 356 for-loop calls _extract_import_aliases on every tree node without filtering on node.type == \"import_directive\". Looks like a deleted-guard regression — the body is over-indented relative to the for header."  # fdea
- op: discuss  # 041a
  at: '2026-05-28T16:59:51Z'  # 041a
  by: agent  # 041a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 041a
  clock: 2  # 041a
  nonce: 041a  # 041a
  message: "Pass 7 dogfooding adds a stronger symptom: the Solidity require-message string 'Not owner' (from BRANCHES_test_solidity.py:114 — require(msg.sender == owner, \"Not owner\")) propagates through the IR/linker chain to produce a synthetic external_symbol node with literal fields {language: \"Not owner\", name: \"Not owner\", canonical_name: \"Not owner:<unknown>:Not owner:Not owner\"}. The bogus 'Not owner' value then leaks into the io-boundaries language-coverage warning as a 'language without I/O primitive catalog'. Node has zero edges so analyses are not corrupted, but the language field has zero validation against a known enum. Reproducible from /tmp/hg-dogfood-2026-05-28/behavior_map.json — see schema_version 0.11.0 graph."  # 041a
- op: discuss  # 6498
  at: '2026-05-28T18:32:30Z'  # 6498
  by: agent  # 6498
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6498
  clock: 3  # 6498
  nonce: '6498'  # 6498
  message: "Pass-9 evidence: the 'Not owner' string-literal-as-import leak now surfaces in io-boundaries JSON output. Running 'hypergumbo io-boundaries --json --input behavior_map.json | jq .unsupported_languages' returns: ['Not owner', 'ansible', 'bash', 'csharp', 'html', 'json', 'markdown', 'solidity', 'sql', 'toml', 'wgsl']. The 'Not owner' entry is the same Solidity require-message-string leak — io-boundaries treats it as a language and adds it to the unsupported list. Downstream consumers of io-boundaries JSON will see this in their unsupported_languages set and confuse it for a real language.\n\nSame root cause (B), broader surface: cli text output (B), language enum count (NN — language count 18 includes 'Not owner'), io-boundaries JSON. Fixing the original Solidity require-msg-as-import resolves all three.\n\nFound in dogfooding pass 9 (2026-05-28)."  # 6498
